    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit requirement in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, the single code path behind `POST /api/owners`:\n\n1. **Added an `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, using the exact logger name the spec and `AuditLogCapture` test helper expect.\n\n2. **Captured the create state** \u2014 recorded `boolean isNew = owner.isNew()` at the top of the method, before `ownerRepository.save(owner)` assigns the id and flips `isNew()` to false.\n\n3. **Emitted the audit line on successful create** \u2014 after the save succeeds, and only when `isNew`, it logs the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n   ```\n   AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-05\n   ```\n\nThe line is emitted only for new owners (not updates), and after the save so the generated `id`, `customerCode`, and business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` are all final and match what `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns.\n\nBoth the new `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test green).",
