    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is small, additive, and idiomatic:\n\n- **Right unit.** Audit logging of a successful create lives naturally in the service method that performs the create, inside the same `@Transactional` boundary. No new class or indirection is warranted for a single log line.\n- **Correct placement of the capture.** `boolean isNew = owner.isNew()` is read at the top because `ownerRepository.save(owner)` assigns the id and flips `isNew()` to false afterward. The audit guard genuinely needs the pre-save value, so the local is justified rather than redundant \u2014 and it reads cleanly next to the post-save `AUDIT.info(...)`.\n- **Idiomatic logging.** A dedicated `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` is the conventional SLF4J way to target a named channel, and the field carries a clear doc comment explaining its purpose. The parameterized `info(...)` call with the three spec fields is standard usage.\n- **No duplication or catch-all growth.** The method is already long, but this adds one guarded block in the same style as the surrounding `owner.isNew()` branches; it doesn't turn the method into a new kind of responsibility sink.\n\nMixing the `isNew` local with the pre-existing inline `owner.isNew()` calls is a cosmetic inconsistency, but those inline calls are all pre-save (where `isNew()` is still valid), so leaving them is defensible and not worth churning.",
